  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8246380",
      "title": "Outsourcing Validation Logic",
      "sourceHash": "0348863818b1d44715538b40b702625c17cd2c46b59526a350013381db7831f6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 4.11,
          "en": "Now, reusing code and simplifying code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.11,
          "end": 8.01,
          "en": "doesn't stop at the custom component level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.01,
          "end": 11.07,
          "en": "because adding such a custom input component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.07,
          "end": 12.63,
          "en": "can definitely help,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.63,
          "end": 17.49,
          "en": "but it's not the only code that could be outsourced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.49,
          "end": 22.143,
          "en": "because what about this validation logic here, for example?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.07,
          "end": 26.73,
          "en": "Obviously these are rather basic checks here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.73,
          "end": 29.4,
          "en": "but still this is logic which we might need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.4,
          "end": 32.22,
          "en": "in different places of the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.22,
          "end": 35.97,
          "en": "For example, if we would add all validation manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.97,
          "end": 38.91,
          "en": "instead of using browser based in features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.91,
          "end": 41.43,
          "en": "we would also have to check the password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.43,
          "end": 44.283,
          "en": "and the email in the signup component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.33,
          "end": 48.12,
          "en": "And therefore, you might want to make",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.12,
          "end": 51.693,
          "en": "that validation logic code reusable as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.65,
          "end": 55.14,
          "en": "And for that, in this starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.14,
          "end": 58.44,
          "en": "I actually already created a util folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.44,
          "end": 61.17,
          "en": "which contains a validation.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.17,
          "end": 64.65,
          "en": "with some example validation functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.65,
          "end": 68.7,
          "en": "that you can consider using in your own projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.7,
          "end": 70.89,
          "en": "And, of course, you can also enhance them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.89,
          "end": 72.45,
          "en": "for those projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.45,
          "end": 76.02,
          "en": "but which we most importantly can also use now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.02,
          "end": 77.40299999999999,
          "en": "in this project here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.78,
          "end": 82.95,
          "en": "For example, isEmail to define this check for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.95,
          "end": 86.97,
          "en": "whether something is an email or not once in this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.97,
          "end": 90.723,
          "en": "and then use it as often and anywhere I need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.8,
          "end": 94.47,
          "en": "For example, in StateLogin.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.47,
          "end": 99.47,
          "en": "I can now import from this util folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.63,
          "end": 101.68,
          "en": "and their validation.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.6,
          "end": 106.38300000000001,
          "en": "and I can import the isEmail, isNotEmpty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.55,
          "end": 111.63300000000001,
          "en": "and hasMinLength validation functions defined there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 113.61,
          "end": 116.43,
          "en": "And we could say that the email is invalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.43,
          "end": 120.48,
          "en": "if it is not an email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 120.48,
          "end": 124.96,
          "en": "And for that, I have to pass my email value to isEmail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 126.45,
          "end": 130.563,
          "en": "And if it is not, not empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 131.7,
          "end": 133.413,
          "en": "so if it is empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 136.98,
          "end": 140.31,
          "en": "That's how we could enhance this validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 140.31,
          "end": 144.75,
          "en": "by outsourcing and reusing the validation logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 144.75,
          "end": 147.66,
          "en": "And we can do the same for the password here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 147.66,
          "end": 150.51,
          "en": "I can check whether we did edit the password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 150.51,
          "end": 155.51,
          "en": "and then if it has a min length and hasMinLength,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 156,
          "end": 159.32999999999998,
          "en": "then once the value which should be checked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 159.32999999999998,
          "end": 163.2,
          "en": "and as a second argument, the minLength we wanna have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 163.2,
          "end": 167.64,
          "en": "And therefore here, I can pass my password as a first value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 167.64,
          "end": 172.35,
          "en": "and then let's say six if I require at least six characters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 172.35,
          "end": 173.94299999999998,
          "en": "as a second value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 175.17000000000002,
          "end": 177.3,
          "en": "And then here we need an exclamation mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 177.3,
          "end": 180.06,
          "en": "because here I wanna check for invalidity,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 180.06,
          "end": 182.43,
          "en": "so if this condition is not met",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 182.43,
          "end": 185.073,
          "en": "because then the password is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 187.98,
          "end": 190.56,
          "en": "And with that, we got this validation code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 190.56,
          "end": 191.82,
          "en": "out of this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 191.82,
          "end": 195.81,
          "en": "And therefore again, we got the same behavior as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 195.81,
          "end": 200.343,
          "en": "but now again achieved by outsourcing and reusing logic.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
